{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"CodeQL","organization":"GitHub","semanticVersion":"2.25.1","notifications":[{"id":"py/baseline/expected-extracted-files","name":"py/baseline/expected-extracted-files","shortDescription":{"text":"Expected extracted files"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Files appearing in the source archive that are expected to be extracted."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true},"properties":{"tags":["expected-extracted-files","telemetry"]}},{"id":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","name":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","shortDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"fullDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}},{"id":"cli/platform","name":"cli/platform","shortDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}}],"rules":[{"id":"py/augur/recurly-client-python/pass3-ssrf","name":"py/augur/recurly-client-python/pass3-ssrf","shortDescription":{"text":"Pass 3: Server-Side Request Forgery (CWE-918)"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Tracks the reviewed CWE-918 input boundaries of the recurly-client-python SDK into its single outbound request funnel. Sources, sinks, barriers and additional taint steps are rendered from the human-reviewed labels in iris/labels/labels.json (run recurly-client-python-ssrf-pass3-20261020, pass 3): 21 source entries (the public-API full-URL parameters of the embedding-application boundary — http_request/element_for_url/headers_for_url/page_for_url/count_for_url/ paginated/put/post; the server-controlled response URL carriers — XML href reads, Location/Link headers; the redemption_code first-path-segment read; the unverified webhook body parameter), 13 sink entries (the http_client.HTTP(S)Connection host argument, the connection.request request-line URL, and the argument-0 URL positions of the funnel), zero sanitizers (verified: no scheme/host allowlist, no private-IP blocking, no redirect validation exists anywhere in the package — resource.py:240-250 only selects the transport), and five additional taint-step families (urljoin both-argument propagation, urlencode query propagation, urlsplit url-to-netloc, ElementTree.fromstring, parse_link_value). The alert message distinguishes full-URL control, host-level control and second-order (server-controlled) carriers; all sources carry classification `candidate` — the SDK boundary set pending host-application context."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-918"],"description":"Tracks the reviewed CWE-918 input boundaries of the\n   recurly-client-python SDK into its single outbound request funnel. Sources,\n   sinks, barriers and additional taint steps are rendered from the\n   human-reviewed labels in iris/labels/labels.json (run\n   recurly-client-python-ssrf-pass3-20261020, pass 3): 21 source entries (the\n   public-API full-URL parameters of the embedding-application boundary —\n   http_request/element_for_url/headers_for_url/page_for_url/count_for_url/\n   paginated/put/post; the server-controlled response URL carriers — XML href\n   reads, Location/Link headers; the redemption_code first-path-segment read;\n   the unverified webhook body parameter), 13 sink entries (the\n   http_client.HTTP(S)Connection host argument, the connection.request\n   request-line URL, and the argument-0 URL positions of the funnel), zero\n   sanitizers (verified: no scheme/host allowlist, no private-IP blocking, no\n   redirect validation exists anywhere in the package — resource.py:240-250\n   only selects the transport), and five additional taint-step families\n   (urljoin both-argument propagation, urlencode query propagation, urlsplit\n   url-to-netloc, ElementTree.fromstring, parse_link_value). The alert message\n   distinguishes full-URL control, host-level control and second-order\n   (server-controlled) carriers; all sources carry classification\n   `candidate` — the SDK boundary set pending host-application context.","id":"py/augur/recurly-client-python/pass3-ssrf","kind":"path-problem","name":"Pass 3: Server-Side Request Forgery (CWE-918)","precision":"low","problem.severity":"error"}}]},"extensions":[{"name":"iris/recurly-client-python-cwe918","semanticVersion":"0.0.1","locations":[{"uri":"file:///C:/Users/lzh/Desktop/github/PyVul-main/iris_manual/SSRF/recurly-client-python/iris/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///C:/Users/lzh/Desktop/github/PyVul-main/iris_manual/SSRF/recurly-client-python/iris/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]},{"name":"codeql/python-all","semanticVersion":"7.0.4","locations":[{"uri":"file:///E:/codeql-codeql-cli-2.25.2/python/ql/lib/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///E:/codeql-codeql-cli-2.25.2/python/ql/lib/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]},{"name":"codeql/threat-models","semanticVersion":"1.0.47","locations":[{"uri":"file:///E:/codeql-codeql-cli-2.25.2/shared/threat-models/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///E:/codeql-codeql-cli-2.25.2/shared/threat-models/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]}]},"invocations":[{"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"recurly/js.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%","index":3}}}],"message":{"text":""},"level":"none","descriptor":{"id":"py/baseline/expected-extracted-files","index":0},"properties":{"formattedMessage":{"text":""}}},{"locations":[{"